Never display the administrator password in the dashboard or return it from an API.

Protect administrative endpoints using server-side authentication and role checks.

Implement rate limiting or other appropriate protection against repeated login attempts.

Validate permissions on the server, not only by hiding buttons in the frontend.

Ensure users cannot access private application records, client enquiries, CVs, or uploaded documents without authorisation.

